Spec: SpecDD Path References

Platform: IntelliJ Platform / Kotlin

Purpose:
  Provide clickable navigation and missing-target warnings for path and glob text in SpecDD files.

Structure:
  SpecDDPathReferenceExtractor.kt: Text-level path and glob candidate extraction.
  SpecDDPathResolver.kt: Project-relative path and glob target resolution.
  SpecDDPathReference.kt: IntelliJ PSI reference for path and glob candidates.
  SpecDDPathReferenceProvider.kt: IntelliJ reference provider.
  SpecDDPathReferenceContributor.kt: IntelliJ reference contributor registration.
  SpecDDPathAnnotator.kt: IntelliJ warning annotator for unresolved path and glob candidates.
  SpecDDCreateFileQuickFix.kt: IntelliJ intention action for creating unresolved exact path references.

Owns:
  references.sdd
  SpecDDPathReferenceExtractor.sdd
  SpecDDPathResolver.sdd
  SpecDDPathReference.sdd
  SpecDDPathReferenceProvider.sdd
  SpecDDPathReferenceContributor.sdd
  SpecDDPathAnnotator.sdd
  SpecDDCreateFileQuickFix.sdd
  SpecDDPathReferenceExtractor.kt
  SpecDDPathResolver.kt
  SpecDDPathReference.kt
  SpecDDPathReferenceProvider.kt
  SpecDDPathReferenceContributor.kt
  SpecDDPathAnnotator.kt
  SpecDDCreateFileQuickFix.kt

Can modify:
  references.sdd
  SpecDDPathReferenceExtractor.sdd
  SpecDDPathResolver.sdd
  SpecDDPathReference.sdd
  SpecDDPathReferenceProvider.sdd
  SpecDDPathReferenceContributor.sdd
  SpecDDPathAnnotator.sdd
  SpecDDCreateFileQuickFix.sdd
  SpecDDPathReferenceExtractor.kt
  SpecDDPathResolver.kt
  SpecDDPathReference.kt
  SpecDDPathReferenceProvider.kt
  SpecDDPathReferenceContributor.kt
  SpecDDPathAnnotator.kt
  SpecDDCreateFileQuickFix.kt

Can read:
  ../parser/*
  ../SpecDDFileType.kt
  ../../../../../../test/kotlin/ai/specdd/idea/references/*

Must:
  Keep path and glob reference behavior separate from structure validation.
  Reuse the shared line classifier for section and key-value detection.
  Extract inline path and glob candidates from task text, scenario steps, key-value lines, and normal body text.
  Extract bare key candidates only from path-bearing key-value sections such as `Structure`.
  Treat path entries as relative to the containing `.sdd` file directory.
  Restrict resolution to files and directories inside the current project root when a project root is available.
  Resolve exact existing files and directories to clickable PSI targets.
  Refresh local VFS entries when mapping resolved paths to PSI targets for navigation.
  Resolve glob patterns to all matching project files or directories.
  Treat malformed glob patterns as unresolved instead of throwing.
  Cap glob results and skip common heavy directories while walking the project tree.
  Register PSI references on the SpecDD PSI text token emitted by the minimal parser.
  Support file-level reference lookup for Go to Declaration on minimal SpecDD PSI files.
  Report warnings, not errors, for path or glob candidates that look like paths but resolve to no target.
  Offer a create-path quick fix for unresolved exact path candidates only.
  Do not offer create-path quick fixes for glob candidates.
  Create missing files or directories only inside the current project root.
  Create missing parent directories when creating a nested exact path.
  Ignore prose-like candidates without path syntax when they resolve to no target.
  Cover extraction, resolution, PSI reference behavior, warning annotations, quick fixes, and contributor registration with tests.

Must not:
  Change parser classification rules.
  Report structural validation errors.
  Define syntax highlighting colors.
  Add user-facing settings.
